    # ── engine 6
    a("## 9. Engine 6 · `add_scale_sign` — the tier-0 value type `ASS` `ESTABLISHED` (the group) · `OURS` (the datatype, the word and the Long Path)\n")
    a(f"Module [`modules/add_scale_sign/`]({GH}modules/add_scale_sign/) (0.3): `maths.py` (`ASS`, `ASSWord`, `group_laws_exact`), `tools.py` (`AddScaleSignModule`, 7 equations), tests `tests/test_add_scale_sign.py` (17; the engine had none before this pass). The type is an element of the affine group Aff(1, ℝ) = ℝ ⋊ (ℝ>0 × ℤ/2): the map x ↦ sign·scale·x + add, composed with `@` (the right factor fires first), inverted with `~`, applied by calling. The naming `ASS` (Add : Scale : Sign) is locked by the author (see the header of `maths.py`).\n")
    a("### 9.1 The group laws, exactly — Convention B\n")
    a("Convention A applies to the class itself (about 250 lines, `ASS` and `ASSWord`: not excerpted). What the paper shows is the one function that tests it: `group_laws_exact` builds eighteen elements from `fractions.Fraction` and checks associativity over all 5832 triples, identity, the two-sided inverse, that SIGN and SCALE commute, and that the group commutators of ADD with SCALE and with SIGN are pure translations. No float appears anywhere in it.\n")
    a(listing("the group laws on an exact grid", "modules/add_scale_sign/maths.py: group_laws_exact", [ASM.group_laws_exact],
              "from typing import Any, Dict\n\nfrom ValaQuenta.modules.add_scale_sign import ASS",
              "print(group_laws_exact())"))
    a("`:CALCULATED`: all seven laws hold on the 18 elements (5832 triples, none fail). Before version 0.2 the manifest claimed exact `Fraction` arithmetic and the inverse did not deliver it: `~` added `0.0` and divided by `1.0`, so a Fraction element came back as floats. The function above is the test that would have caught it, and `~` now keeps the type (ledger X-70).\n")
    a("### 9.2 The bracket — Convention D\n")
    a(transcript("the commutator of ADD with SCALE and with SIGN", "from ValaQuenta.modules.add_scale_sign import ASS\nA, S, G = ASS.ADD(3), ASS.SCALE(2), ASS.SIGN(-1)\ncomm = lambda x, y: ~x @ ~y @ x @ y\nprint(comm(A, S), comm(A, G), comm(S, G))\nprint(S @ A, A @ S)"))
    a("The group commutator x⁻¹y⁻¹xy of ADD(a) with SCALE(s) is the translation a·(1/s − 1) and of ADD(a) with SIGN(−1) the translation −2a, and SCALE commutes with SIGN. This is `[SCALE, ADD] = ADD` as a statement about the group: order matters at this tier only through the offset. (The other convention for the commutator gives the negated translation.)\n")
    a("### 9.3 The word is a readout, not a homomorphism — Convention D\n")
    a(transcript("u of a composite against the sum of u", "from ValaQuenta.modules.add_scale_sign import ASS\na, b = ASS(1.5, 2.0, 1), ASS(0.5, 3.0, -1)\nprint(round((a @ b).u(), 6), round(a.u() + b.u(), 6))\nw = (a @ b).lineage('chrono')\nprint(round(w.u_total(), 6), round(w.u_sum_of_steps(), 6), round(w.firing_defect(), 6))"))
    a("The word u = g·ln s + a is a number read off one element; it does not add under composition. The sum in the wiki's u = Σ[gₖ ln sₖ + aₖ] runs over the recorded steps (`u_sum_of_steps`), and the firing defect (g − 1)·ln s is zero exactly when g = +1 or s = 1. The wiki wording was corrected in this pass.\n")
    a("### 9.4 Interactive visualizations\n")
    a("`gallery/add_scale_sign/` ([index](" + GH.replace("blob/main/", "tree/main/") + "gallery/add_scale_sign)): five pages, raw Canvas 2D, no libraries, no network, each with an *About this visual* panel and a self-check that recomputes the word, the fold, both Smith coordinates, the group commutators, the Long Path of four words (chrono and zeta) and the exact grid in rational arithmetic, and compares them with the numbers the Python engine baked into `ass_data.js`.\n")
    a("| page | shows | measured on load |\n|---|---|---|\n| `canvas2d_plane.html` | two elements as lines, the composites X∘Y and Y∘X, fixed points, a cobweb | commutators agree at 9 parameter pairs |\n| `canvas2d_bracket.html` | the commutator walked on a number line; the translation a·(1/s − 1) against ln s | translation, identity cases |\n| `canvas2d_fold.html` | u, Γ, Γ_SCALE east–west, Γ_ADD north–south, the sign sheet, the firing defect | 32 points, max difference 9e-16 |\n| `canvas2d_longpath.html` | trajectory, collisions, the flip test, chrono against zeta order | 4 words, both orders |\n| `canvas2d_grouptable.html` | an exact 18-element window: commuting pairs, closure, offsets | 5832 triples, 76 / 324 commute, 84 inside |\n")
