    a("## 14. Conclusion\n")
    a("Engine 0 fixes the constants once; engine 1 documents Ĥ_RB through the sigma_rb map (ψ in, sigma_rb out), its tests, its flow and its failure modes; engine 2 reads the Tier 0 constants at their σ-facets and withdraws what the record withdrew; engine 3 is the one implementation of the Hyperwebster address and the T32/GF(2) algebra, with its square law, its detector and, for the claim it once carried, the control it lacked; engine 4 proves the one finite theorem under the \"N-shape\" claim (the Niemeier gap) and records, with exact controls, what around it is only arithmetic; engine 5 derives the 42 assessors and seven box-kites from the Cayley–Dickson table alone, replaces a quoted group order by the enumerated one (1344 = 8 · 168, non-split), and shows five pictures that recompute their own numbers. Each later engine is added the same way and regenerated by `paper/make_paper.py`.\n")
